id: pm-gzr4j6
title: "Ecosystem Daily Release jobs hold a hosted runner for up to 360 minutes waiting on their own release PR's queued CI, and ecosystem CI never cancels superseded runs, so the account's 20 runner slots starve every repository"
description: "Runner-held waits occur in both ecosystem release/CI templates and the pm-cli exact-tag recovery parent. Ecosystem daily release jobs have opened a release PR and waited for its queued checks while occupying a hosted runner. The pm-cli Auto Release parent has also waited in-job on an independently dispatched Release child, retaining a runner while the child acceptance jobs were queued. Shared personal-account capacity and uncanceled duplicate CI matrices amplify these waits. Durable remediation must cover both scopes: event-driven publication or observation without a runner-held dependency wait, per-ref PR CI concurrency, and staggered ecosystem cron windows. Ordinary long-running tests are not automatically evidence of a deadlock."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: ci,ecosystem,github-actions,release,runner-queue
created_at: "2026-10-30T15:20:19.395Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-13T01:15:49.618Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: Neither ecosystem release jobs nor the pm-cli exact-tag recovery parent hold a hosted runner while waiting for independently dispatched children or queued PR checks; Publication and completion handling use merge or workflow completion events while preserving existing child identity and original failure observations; Ecosystem CI declares workflow-and-ref concurrency with cancellation of superseded pull-request runs; Ecosystem release cron windows are staggered so separate repositories do not begin within the same five-minute window; An account-wide snapshot one hour after a release window finds no ecosystem or pm-cli parent waiting in-job for its own PR checks or child workflow
parent: pm-doxj
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: GitHub Free personal account unbraind shared by about 30 public repositories
expected_result: Ecosystem release workflows and the pm-cli exact-tag recovery parent do not hold a runner while waiting for independent PR checks or child workflows. CI concurrency cancels superseded PR runs and ecosystem cron windows are staggered.
actual_result: "Historical 2026-10-30 starvation observations remain in comments/history. On 2026-11-09 the pm-cli parent 42599219606 waited on independent child 42601586640 for over four hours; only that redundant parent was canceled after verifying the child producer had succeeded. The child and immutable publication identities were preserved. The 16:35 UTC census covered 172 non-archived owner repositories and found ten workflows with sixteen executing Ubuntu jobs, including advancing ordinary CI steps. No unrelated workflow was canceled. Durable decoupling, concurrency and cron changes remain unimplemented under this open owner."
component: ecosystem-release
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-m6ig79,related,"2026-10-30T15:20:19.395Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-30T17:14:11.623Z","harness:claude-code","2026-10-30 17:15 UTC queue census across all unbraind repos: about 90 queued runs against the 20-job account cap and zero pm-cli jobs in progress. 45 of the queued runs were Dependabot dynamic update jobs, mostly repeats of the same directory update (PersonalAgent pip 10+10, arXiv-PyG-new uv 7, Tokenwerk uv 5). Cancelled the 31 superseded queued Dependabot runs, keeping the newest per repository and directory. Repeated Dependabot update jobs are a second source of runner starvation beside the release merge waits; a durable fix needs grouped Dependabot updates or open-pull-request limits in those repositories."
  "2026-11-09T10:03:46.566Z","harness:codex","2026-11-09 10:02 UTC read-only queue census across the 100 most recently active owner repositories: 41 queued runs and seven in-progress workflows, with multiple hosted jobs per workflow. pm-cli PR #1696 still has required coverage/static jobs waiting after build foundation and native macOS acceptance passed. Current holders include long-running npm/Bun release-gate/test steps and one gated-sync dispatch step; this census does not prove they are deadlocked or superseded. No unrelated workflow was canceled, and no publishing state was changed. Sanitized census retained locally for the existing canonical capacity owner."
  "2026-11-09T12:53:48.167Z","harness:codex","2026-11-09 12:54 UTC follow-up to the earlier seven-workflow holder census: five original holders have completed (four successful, one failed), one workflow is now queued and one CI workflow has a currently executing test step. This demonstrates progress rather than proving a persistent deadlock. The current PR still waited twenty minutes with its foundation queued, but none of these unrelated workflows was canceled and no publication state was altered."
  "2026-11-09T14:47:06.548Z","harness:codex","2026-11-09 14:44 UTC own-repository instance of the runner-held dependency wait: pm-cli Auto Release parent 42599219606 was waiting on independently dispatched Release 42601586640 for over four hours. The child producer had succeeded while its publication verification remained queued. Canceled only the redundant parent watcher after confirming these states; parent is terminal canceled and the child remains preserved. No other repository run was canceled. This demonstrates that the durable decoupling work must also cover the pm-cli exact-tag recovery watcher, without treating canceled observations as successful release evidence."
  "2026-11-09T16:37:06.903Z","harness:codex","2026-11-09 16:35 UTC read-only census covers all 172 non-archived owner repositories without API errors: ten workflows have sixteen executing Ubuntu jobs; pm-cli has no executing workflow. These holders are CI/release-gate/test/CodeQL steps, not identified runner-held release-PR watchers, and several began new steps around 16:30-16:33. Two pm-vcs CI workflows share one head, but this observation alone does not establish safe cancellation of another repository workstream. No unrelated run was canceled. Native twenty-minute waits remain the delivery gate; the durable template/concurrency issue remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-11-13T01:15:49.617Z","harness:claude-code","Observed again 2026-11-12, during the evening fleet release wave. PR 1714's CI (head 2bbb1c41e, pushed 21:04Z) waited about 60 minutes for its foundation build. Its Ubuntu fan-out jobs, created at 22:04Z, stayed queued until about 23:40Z, and its security jobs, created at 21:04Z, until about 23:30Z.\nCensuses:\n- 21:30Z: 18 of the 20 account slots were running fleet pull_request CI.\n- 23:00Z: 20 of 20 slots were running fleet Ubuntu jobs: release/2026.11.12 PRs on pm-ado, pm-csv and pm-jira; push-to-main CI on pm-github, pm-ts-starter, pm-web and pm-todos; Daily Release runs on pm-ado, pm-vcs and pm-ts-starter; and three feature-branch PRs.\nThe fleet session held its dispatch and cancelled 12 of its own queued runs at 21:35Z, but the hold expired at 22:29Z before pm-cli's jobs had started. At 23:01Z I cancelled 15 fleet feature-branch pull_request runs (no release, push, schedule, dispatch or Dependabot runs). After PR 1714 merged at 00:35Z on 2026-11-13, I re-ran the 6 whose PR head was unchanged; the other 9 had been superseded by newer pushes. Jobs created later on other repositories started before pm-cli's earlier-created jobs, so per-label queueing across repositories is not FIFO by creation time. A hold that ends at a fixed time therefore does not protect a PR whose fan-out starts late.\n"
